    "description": "Cross-Sound Cable owns and operates a high-voltage direct-current submarine transmission link between Connecticut and Long Island. Its customer base is the regional power system, with transmission capacity sold under contractual arrangements that support interregional power transfers and grid reliability. The asset uses a contracted infrastructure model rather than retail utility service, with revenues linked to the availability and use of transmission capacity. Public materials describe a 24-mile, 330-megawatt HVDC cable connecting the New England and Long Island electric grids. The project has operated since the early 2000s and remains a strategic interconnector between ISO New England and New York load centers. AIA Energy, an Argo-managed vehicle backed by institutional investors including APG and CalSTRS, acquired Cross-Sound Cable in 2015, although current ownership percentages are not publicly disclosed.",
